<%# Project Update Report (module 8 part 8.10; PRD §4.4, §5.4).

    WHAT THIS SCREEN HAS TO MAKE OBVIOUS

    1. APPROVING FREEZES THE PERIOD. Under owner decision A (2026-10-04) the approval and the freeze
       are the same act. The approve control says so in the button's own label and in the warning
       above it — a Project Manager must not close a month by surprise.
    2. THE REPORT COMPILES, IT DOES NOT COMPUTE. Every figure is read from the service that owns the
       rule, so this screen cannot disagree with the forecast, revenue or aging screens. Said in
       words at the foot, not just claimed in code.
    3. A POSITION IS DATED. If the month has no measurement of its own, the report quotes the last
       measured month and SAYS SO. It never prints 0 for "not measured".
    4. `status` IS THE WORKFLOW: draft → reviewed → frozen. There is no separate "approved" resting
       state, because approving IS the freeze.

    Receives: project, month, stored (the saved row or null), live (the compiled body),
    stale, caps, periods, error, notice, saved. %>
<% if (typeof error !== 'undefined' && error) { %>
<div class="errb"><div class="errb-tx"><p><b>Not done.</b> <%= error %></p></div></div>
<% } %>
<% if (typeof notice !== 'undefined' && notice) { %>
<div class="note ok"><svg><use href="#i-check"/></svg><b>Done.</b> <%= notice %></div>
<% } %>

<% if (!project) { %>
<div class="card"><div class="fbody">
  <p><b>No project is in scope for your account, so there is no report to show.</b></p>
  <p class="dim" style="margin:6px 0 0">Ask an Administrator to assign you to a project.</p>
</div></div>
<% } else { %>

<% const pct = (n) => (n === null || n === undefined ? null : Number(n).toFixed(2)); %>
<% const isFrozen = periods.isFrozen(project.id, month); %>
<% const status = stored ? stored.status : null; %>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-hd">
    <h2><%= month %> · Project update report</h2>
    <span class="r">
      <% if (!stored) { %><span class="chip nt">NOT COMPILED</span>
      <% } else if (status === 'frozen') { %><span class="chip ok">FROZEN</span>
      <% } else if (status === 'reviewed') { %><span class="chip wn">REVIEWED</span>
      <% } else { %><span class="chip nt">DRAFT</span><% } %>
      <% if (isFrozen) { %> <span class="chip ok">PERIOD FROZEN</span>
      <% } else { %> <span class="chip nt">PERIOD OPEN</span><% } %>
    </span>
  </div>
  <% if (stored) { %>
  <%# Module 8 part 8.11: the exports. They download the STORED report — the record — not a live
      recomputation, so the file matches what was approved. A draft says DRAFT on its face. %>
  <div class="fbody" style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)">
    <span class="dim" style="margin-right:8px">Download this report:</span>
    <a class="btn" href="/reports/update/<%= stored.id %>/export.pdf">PDF</a>
    <a class="btn" href="/reports/update/<%= stored.id %>/export.xlsx">Excel</a>
    <span class="dim" style="margin-left:8px"><%= status === 'draft'
      ? 'This is a draft, so the file is marked DRAFT.'
      : 'The file carries the stored figures and who approved it.' %></span>
  </div>
  <% } %>
  <div class="fbody">
    <p class="dim" style="margin:0">
      <b>What this is.</b> The monthly position report for <%= month %>: schedule and cost
      performance, what the client owes against what has been recognised, what the project owes,
      the exceptions this period, and what changed in the baseline.
      <%= periods.isFrozen(project.id, month)
        ? 'This period is frozen, so backdated entries to it are refused — the figures below are the period\u2019s history.'
        : 'Approving this report will freeze the period: after that, backdated entries to ' + month + ' are refused.' %>
    </p>
    <% if (stale && status !== 'frozen') { %>
    <p style="margin:10px 0 0"><b class="wn">The stored report is out of date.</b>
      Something changed after it was compiled
      (<%= stored.spi === live.spi ? '' : 'SPI ' %>). Regenerate it to bring it up to date.
    </p>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="grid k4">
  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-chart"/></svg>Schedule (SPI)</div>
    <div class="v mono"><%= pct(live.spi) === null ? 'Not measured' : pct(live.spi) %></div>
    <div class="f"><%= live.spi === null
      ? 'No month at or before this one has been measured yet.'
      : 'Earned ÷ planned, to date · as at ' + live.measured_month %></div></div>

  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-chart"/></svg>Cost (CPI)</div>
    <div class="v mono"><%= pct(live.cpi) === null ? 'Not measured' : pct(live.cpi) %></div>
    <div class="f"><%= live.cpi === null
      ? 'No month at or before this one has been measured yet.'
      : 'Earned ÷ actual, to date · as at ' + live.measured_month %></div></div>

  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-cash"/></svg>Receivable</div>
    <div class="v mono"><%= fmt(live.receivable_amount) %></div>
    <div class="f">what the client still owes
      <%= live.receivable_undated ? ' · plus ' + fmt(live.receivable_undated) + ' not yet datable' : '' %></div></div>

  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-book"/></svg>Revenue recognised</div>
    <div class="v mono"><%= fmt(live.revenue_recognized) %></div>
    <div class="f"><%= live.method
      ? 'to date, under the ' + live.method + ' method'
      : 'no revenue method is set, so nothing is recognised' %></div></div>
</div>

<% if (live.evm_stale) { %>
<div class="note" style="margin-top:12px">
  <svg><use href="#i-info"/></svg>
  <span><b>The performance figures are dated <%= live.measured_month %>, not <%= month %>.</b>
    This month has no progress recorded and no cost booked, so nothing has been measured in it. The
    report quotes the latest position that WAS measured at or before it, rather than printing zero —
    a zero would read as "exactly on plan", which is a different claim from "not measured".</span>
</div>
<% } %>

<div class="card" style="margin-top:12px">
  <div class="card-hd">
    <h2>Exceptions this period</h2>
    <span class="r">PRD §4.4 · threshold <%= live.exceptions.spiThreshold %> SPI / <%= live.exceptions.cpiThreshold %> CPI</span>
  </div>
  <div class="fbody">
    <% if (!live.exceptions.raised.length) { %>
    <p><b>Nothing from the alert list fired for this project.</b></p>
    <% } else { %>
    <ul style="margin:0 0 4px;padding-left:18px">
      <% live.exceptions.raised.forEach(function(e) { %>
      <li style="margin:0 0 6px"><span class="chip wn">CHECK</span> <%= e.text %></li>
      <% }); %>
    </ul>
    <% } %>
    <% if (live.exceptions.notEvaluated.length) { %>
    <p class="dim" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      <b>Not checked:</b>
      <% live.exceptions.notEvaluated.forEach(function(e, i) { %><%= i ? '; ' : '' %><%= e.kind.replace(/_/g, ' ') %> — <%= e.reason %><% }); %>.
      An alert that cannot be evaluated is named here rather than left out, because an absent line
      would read as "no problem".
    </p>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top:12px">
  <div class="card-hd"><h2>Baseline — what changed</h2><span class="r">PRD §5.4 · prior baseline vs current</span></div>
  <div class="fbody">
    <p style="margin:0 0 8px"><%= live.baseline_changes.note %></p>
    <% if (live.baseline_changes.rows.length) { %>
    <div class="tw"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Reference</th><th>Change</th><th>Title</th>
        <th style="text-align:right">Cost impact</th><th>Effective</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      <% live.baseline_changes.rows.forEach(function(b) { %>
        <tr>
          <td class="mono"><%= b.bcr_no || '#' + b.id %></td>
          <td><%= b.change_type.replace(/_/g, ' ') %></td>
          <td><%= b.title %></td>
          <td class="mono" style="text-align:right"><%= fmt(b.impact_cost) %></td>
          <td class="mono"><%= b.effective_period || '—' %></td>
        </tr>
      <% }); %>
      </tbody>
      <tfoot><tr><th colspan="3">Total impact this period</th>
        <th class="mono" style="text-align:right"><%= fmt(live.baseline_changes.totalImpact) %></th>
        <th></th></tr></tfoot>
    </table></div>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top:12px">
  <div class="card-hd">
    <h2>The report and the period</h2>
    <span class="r">record → review → approve, and the approval freezes <%= month %></span>
  </div>
  <div class="fbody">
    <% if (!stored) { %>
      <p><b>This month has not been compiled yet.</b> Compiling produces a <b>draft</b> — it changes
      nothing and closes nothing. Drafts can be regenerated as the month's figures move.</p>
      <% if (caps.canManageReport) { %>
      <form method="post" action="/reports/update/generate">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
        <input type="hidden" name="period_month" value="<%= month %>">
        <button class="btn pri" type="submit"><svg><use href="#i-plus"/></svg>Compile this month's report</button>
      </form>
      <% } else { %>
      <p class="dim" style="margin:8px 0 0">Compiling the report is a Project Controller, Project
        Manager or Project Admin task.</p>
      <% } %>

    <% } else if (status === 'draft') { %>
      <p><b>Draft.</b> A Controller reviews it, then the Project Manager approves it — and that
      approval is what freezes <%= month %>.</p>
      <% if (caps.canManageReport) { %>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:8px">
        <form method="post" action="/reports/update/<%= stored.id %>/review">
          <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
          <button class="btn pri" type="submit">Mark reviewed</button>
        </form>
        <form method="post" action="/reports/update/generate">
          <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
          <input type="hidden" name="period_month" value="<%= month %>">
          <button class="btn" type="submit">Regenerate from current figures</button>
        </form>
      </div>
      <% } %>

    <% } else if (status === 'reviewed') { %>
      <p style="margin:0 0 8px"><b class="wn">Reviewed and waiting for the Project Manager.</b></p>
      <% if (caps.canApproveReport) { %>
      <div class="errb" style="margin:0 0 10px"><div class="errb-tx"><p style="margin:0">
        <b>Approving freezes <%= month %>.</b> After this, entries dated in <%= month %> are refused by
        the system and must be tagged to the next period. That is the point of the freeze — the
        report stays truthful — but it cannot be done by accident. It can be undone on the
        Accounting periods screen if a correction is genuinely needed.
      </p></div></div>
      <form method="post" action="/reports/update/<%= stored.id %>/approve">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
        <button class="btn pri" type="submit">Approve and freeze <%= month %></button>
      </form>
      <% } else { %>
      <p class="dim" style="margin:0">A Project Manager approves this — and the approval freezes the
      period, which is why it is not the compiler's decision.</p>
      <% } %>

    <% } else { %>
      <p><b>The period <%= month %> is frozen and this report is its record.</b>
      <% if (stored.approved_at) { %>Approved <%= String(stored.approved_at).slice(0, 10) %>.<% } %>
      Its figures cannot be regenerated: a frozen report is what the period reported, and rewriting
      it would silently erase a variance.</p>
      <p class="dim" style="margin:8px 0 0">
        To change the underlying entries, reopen the period on the
        <a href="/periods">Accounting periods</a> screen first. That is an Administrator act and it
        is audited.
      </p>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top:12px">
  <div class="card-hd"><h2>The figures on this report</h2><span class="r">positions to date</span></div>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Figure</th><th style="text-align:right">Value</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Schedule performance (SPI)</td>
        <td class="mono" style="text-align:right"><%= pct(live.spi) === null ? '—' : pct(live.spi) %></td>
        <td class="dim">earned value ÷ planned value, cumulative<%= live.measured_month ? ' as at ' + live.measured_month : '' %></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cost performance (CPI)</td>
        <td class="mono" style="text-align:right"><%= pct(live.cpi) === null ? '—' : pct(live.cpi) %></td>
        <td class="dim">earned value ÷ actual cost, cumulative<%= live.measured_month ? ' as at ' + live.measured_month : '' %></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cost variance</td>
        <td class="mono" style="text-align:right"><%= live.cost_variance_pct === null ? '—' : (live.cost_variance_pct > 0 ? '+' : '') + live.cost_variance_pct + '%' %></td>
        <td class="dim">(actual − earned) ÷ earned · <b>positive means over budget</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Receivable</td>
        <td class="mono" style="text-align:right"><%= fmt(live.receivable_amount) %></td>
        <td class="dim">what the client still owes, from the aging list</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Revenue recognised</td>
        <td class="mono" style="text-align:right"><%= fmt(live.revenue_recognized) %></td>
        <td class="dim">cumulative, under the configured method<%= live.method ? ' (' + live.method + ')' : '' %></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Payable</td>
        <td class="mono" style="text-align:right"><%= fmt(live.payable_amount) %></td>
        <td class="dim">what the project owes, from the ledger</td></tr>
      <% if (live.recognition && live.recognition.period_amount) { %>
      <tr><td>Recognised this month</td>
        <td class="mono" style="text-align:right"><%= fmt(live.recognition.period_amount) %></td>
        <td class="dim">the movement in the month, not the position
          <%= live.recognition.period_basis_pct === null ? '' : '· ' + live.recognition.period_basis_pct + '% of contract' %></td></tr>
      <% } %>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <div class="fbody">
    <p class="dim" style="margin:0">Every figure above is read from the service that owns its rule —
      the forecast service for SPI and CPI, the revenue service for recognition, the aging list for
      receivables. Nothing is worked out twice here, so this report cannot disagree with the screens
      it is read beside. The approved plan is never changed by anything on this page.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<% } %>
